  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-AECID HUMANITAIRE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated response to the urgent priority needs of internally displaced people and hosts affected by the security and climate crises in Diffa, Niger.
Niger and the HRP 2023, the aim of the project is to meet the priority needs of women and men affectedby the security and climate crises, by improving food and nutritional security and strengthening people&apos;s ability to protect themselves in theDiffa region of Niger. The 16-month project will be implemented by Oxfam and Garkua in the communes of Bosso andToumour (Bosso department) and will target a total of 15,000 people (9,000 women and 6,000 men). Through this project, Oxfam and Garkua hope to generate the following positive impacts on the people of the Diffa region: 1) Strengthen food and nutritionalsecurity for 12,500 people (7,500 women and 5,000 men); 2) Improve access to community protection services for 2,500 people (1,500 women and 1,000 men).</narrative>
  </description>
